[SPEAKER_00]: obsession? Or does it remain a focused approach to something without it becoming something in which you're behaving like a maniac? Once again,

31:50.503 --> 32:01.462
[SPEAKER_00]: the seed is always there. It's difficult to draw a very fine line that at one end of the border, You are being focused and working hard. In the

32:01.502 --> 32:12.907
[SPEAKER_00]: other case, you become so obsessed that you are now losing control over your life and your energies and your drive by this aspect. Once again, a

32:12.947 --> 32:20.954
[SPEAKER_00]: very personal thing. Imagine the amount of time an astronaut, somebody who's actually gone to space, how much time they have spent in the

32:20.974 --> 32:30.993
[SPEAKER_00]: ground. You look at the first few guys, the Apollo fellows, Neil Armstrong and Buzz, and these guys have spent years Two to three years,

32:31.093 --> 32:39.399
[SPEAKER_00]: four years of 10 hours a day working at something which is a one-time event of going to space. A lot of hard work. A lot of hard work. It's not

32:39.459 --> 32:50.127
[SPEAKER_00]: seen. It's all behind the lines. Those guys who achieve big feats, some of the stuff that they do themselves, they may not admit how much effort

32:50.147 --> 32:59.909
[SPEAKER_00]: has actually gone in. A lot more than what is visible, actually. So to conclude this, it's basically look at how bad you want it and then look at

33:00.810 --> 33:13.054
[SPEAKER_01]: how bad can you actually want it considering your realities. Yes. You draw the line between risk and reward. If you find that your so-called

33:13.154 --> 33:24.209
[SPEAKER_00]: drive is taking a bend when your own life doesn't matter to you and you are ready to risk it beyond a certain point, especially considering the

33:24.249 --> 33:34.306
[SPEAKER_00]: number of variables that are beyond your control. It's a really tough call. I love the finishing touch that you gave on there because I think

33:34.446 --> 33:43.729
[SPEAKER_01]: that will answer a lot of curiosities for everybody who's going ahead into any passion or any meaning in their life. But while we are talking

