[SPEAKER_01]: humans and paragliding can be considered as a team sport, but at the end, it is simply an individual sport when it comes to controlling your

34:03.239 --> 34:16.126
[SPEAKER_01]: aircraft and making decisions in the air. Does a person need to focus on finding a team or a tribe? Or is it that you will have to find your own

34:16.186 --> 34:27.393
[SPEAKER_01]: motivation and stick to it? So support system, how and when does one identify a need for it? And if yes, then how do you start working towards

34:27.473 --> 34:37.218
[SPEAKER_01]: it? Different sports have different support systems. And in terms of baggling, it all boils down to two or three different aspects. Firstly,

34:38.199 --> 34:46.388
[SPEAKER_00]: if you're in the sport for the fun and excitement, then just the camaraderie is good enough for the time spent hanging around on the

34:46.428 --> 34:54.357
