34:54.417 --> 35:02.523
[SPEAKER_00]: You may know that the first takeoff window is at about let's say 11 o'clock in the morning and you don't need more than let's say half an hour

35:02.803 --> 35:11.705
[SPEAKER_00]: 45 minutes to go up there assess the weather get your gear in order before you take off but people still go up at 8 39 and you see them hanging around

35:11.845 --> 35:20.547
[SPEAKER_00]: at the local restaurant or tea shop knowing jolly well that they're going to do nothing for the next two hours before they fly and

35:20.587 --> 35:30.998
[SPEAKER_00]: interestingly that discussion they have there only 10 to 15 percent of it may relate to And maybe otherwise just general banter. But people do

35:31.058 --> 35:38.381
[SPEAKER_00]: it and they do it regularly. So it indicates that there's a lot more to something where there's a support system per se from the point of view of

