43:05.827 --> 43:12.451
[SPEAKER_00]: therefore I'll charge one fifth, then that's fine. But if you're charging the same amount and then not doing it, then I think ethically

43:12.511 --> 43:22.392
[SPEAKER_00]: it's incorrect. I think ethics, of course, is coming from the point of a seller who's selling it. But we are circling back to the analogy that you

43:22.412 --> 43:29.397
[SPEAKER_01]: made in the beginning that see how willing the person is to share. Or maybe I think you mentioned his body language because you can judge a lot

43:29.417 --> 43:36.584
[SPEAKER_01]: from that and identify behavior from the way they behave and the way they're trying to sell you the product. or even a web shop for that

43:36.644 --> 43:45.434
[SPEAKER_01]: matter, the information on the web shop, how transparent it is. Once you try and read it, once you dig deep into it, you will see these small hints

43:45.554 --> 43:54.203
[SPEAKER_01]: here and there, which give you enough clues to make a wise decision. And I have been on the end. where I haven't made very wise decisions. So that's

43:54.223 --> 44:03.609
[SPEAKER_01]: why I just made it a point that every time I get a chance, I speak about this to my audiences that it's very difficult to find a sweet spot where you

44:04.469 --> 44:13.494
[SPEAKER_01]: don't offend them yet. You try and understand how much you can trust them because they're obviously more senior, more airtime, more legacy

